      "writtenOn": "2026-08-17T09:27:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we share the existing TSO builder instead of maintaining a second implementation for eMPW? The two versions have already drifted: `rdma_mlx5_try_tso()` falls back to regular SEND when `pkt_sz \u003c hdr_sz`, while this version reports `TSO_PAYLOAD_TOO_BIG` and drops the packet. Ideally the common builder would return the resulting buffer index, WQEBB count, last control segment, and status, leaving the legacy and eMPW callers to apply their different ring accounting.",
      "revId": "e426b6079f2b46961be88d7a26fa4a8077894321",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
